<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Muzong of Liao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">931–969</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Yelü Jing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Muzong of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a>, born Yelü Jing, reigned from 951 to 969. Remembered for his heavy drinking and long sleeps, he neglected government and ruled harshly over his attendants, by whom he was murdered in 969. His reign saw the Liao lose some southern territory to the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/later-zhou">Later Zhou</a>.</p></div>
